# ARTICLES and full article pages
articles=[('a-faith-that-shows-up','A faith that shows up.','Christian living','James 1:22–25','Faith grows as we respond to God’s Word in ordinary moments.',[
('Start with listening.','A full week can leave us hearing many voices and paying attention to very few. James calls us to receive God’s Word with humility. Before asking what everyone else should change, we can begin with a quieter question: What is God showing me? Reading slowly, noticing the context, and praying over a passage help us listen with care.'),
('Choose one faithful response.','James warns against hearing without doing. We can agree with a message about forgiveness and still hold tightly to resentment. We can admire generosity without sharing what we have. A faithful response may begin with one concrete act: make the phone call, tell the truth, offer help, or ask forgiveness. Obedience takes shape in the life we already live.'),
('Keep walking with others.','We need people who will encourage us and ask how we are doing. Share one thing you are learning with a trusted Christian friend or Bible study group. Invite them to pray with you. Growth often looks like small, repeated steps taken in dependence on God, with a community beside us.'),
('A question for this week.','What is one clear response you can make to the Scripture you have been reading? Bring it to God in prayer, then take that next step.')]),
('praying-in-an-ordinary-week','Praying in an ordinary week.','Prayer','Philippians 4:6–7','Bring the life you actually have into conversation with God.',[
('Begin where you are.','Prayer does not require a polished speech. In Philippians 4, Paul invites believers to bring their requests to God with thanksgiving. The worries that follow us through a workday, a family conversation, or an uncertain season are things we can bring before Him. We do not have to pretend they are small.'),
('Make room for thanksgiving.','Thanksgiving helps us remember God’s care while our questions remain. Name a grace you have received: a person who listened, strength for a difficult day, forgiveness in Christ, or a need that was met. Gratitude gives us a way to acknowledge God’s faithfulness without denying the weight of what we face.'),
('Pray with someone.','A simple request can open the door to shared care. Tell a trusted friend what is weighing on you, and ask how you can pray for them. A church prayer gathering gives us space to carry one another’s burdens and look beyond our own needs to the church, our neighbours, and the world.'),
('A simple place to start.','Set aside a few quiet minutes today. Thank God for one thing, name one burden, and pray for one person. Return to the passage and let its invitation guide you.')]),
('making-room-for-community','Making room for community.','Church life','Acts 2:42–47','Shared life grows through ordinary habits of worship, care, and fellowship.',[
('Give attention to what matters.','Acts 2 describes believers devoted to the apostles’ teaching, fellowship, breaking bread, and prayer. Their shared life had a clear center. They listened to the truth about Jesus and learned to live as His people. Community grows as we make room for these practices together.'),
('Take the first small step.','Getting to know people can feel awkward, especially when life is busy or you are new to a church. Start simply. Learn a name. Stay for a conversation. Join a Bible study. Offer to help with something practical. Relationships usually deepen through repeated moments of attention.'),
('Notice who needs care.','The early church’s fellowship included practical generosity. We can ask who is absent, who is under pressure, and who may need company. A meal, a message, a ride, or a listening ear can become a meaningful expression of Christ’s love. Ask before assuming what another person needs.'),
('An invitation for this week.','Choose one way to make room for another person. Pray for them, reach out, and follow through. Shared life takes time, and these ordinary steps help us grow together.')])]
body=hero('Faith for<br>everyday life.','Biblical reflections for following Jesus through ordinary days, honest questions, and life together.')
body+='<section class="section gray-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="article-list">'+''.join(f'<article><div class="article-index">0{i+1}</div><div><p class="article-topic">{topic} · {ref}</p><h2>{title}</h2><p>{desc}</p>{link(slug+".html","Read the reflection","text-link")}</div></article>' for i,(slug,title,topic,ref,desc,parts) in enumerate(articles))+'</div></div></section>'+cta('Hear the Word, too.','Listen to messages from Faith Life throughout your week.','messages.html','Explore messages')
